# Changelog

Changes in reverse chronological order.

## 2026-07-10

- `Value` enum (Phase 1, `sc-query`): landed the universal row value type that
  the rest of the query AST is built on (technical design §4). A single
  `serde`-serializable enum with the twelve MVP variants — `Null`, `Bool`,
  `Int(i64)`, `Float(f64)`, `Text(String)`, `Bytes(Vec<u8>)`,
  `Json(serde_json::Value)`, `Uuid`, `Date(NaiveDate)`, `Time(NaiveTime)`,
  `Timestamp(DateTime<Utc>)` (maps to `timestamptz`), and `Decimal` (maps to
  `numeric`). JSON is a first-class variant per the design, not an add-on. The
  enum is `PartialEq` but deliberately not `Eq`/`Hash` because `f64` has no
  total order/equality. Added ergonomic `From` conversions for each backing type
  (plus `&str`, `i32`, and `Option<T> → Null`) and small accessors
  (`is_null`, `kind`, `as_text`/`as_int`/`as_bool`). Serialised with an
  externally-tagged `{ "type", "value" }` shape so a statement stays inspectable
  and reconstructable by code adapters. Pulled `serde`, `serde_json`, `uuid`,
  `chrono`, and `rust_decimal` (all already pinned in `[workspace.dependencies]`)
  into `sc-query`. Unit tests cover the `From` conversions, `Option`→`Null`
  mapping, accessors, the stable serde tag shape, and JSON round-trips of every
  rich variant (uuid/date/time/timestamp/decimal). `cargo fmt --check` and
  `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings` both pass clean on the crate.
- Integration-test harness (Phase 0): added a shared helper crate
  `sc-test-harness` under `tests/harness` (workspace member, `publish = false`)
  implementing the "real Postgres, reset per test" strategy from the technical
  design (principle 4). `TestDb::new()` creates a **freshly named, empty
  database per test** (`sc_test_<uuid>`) from a maintenance connection and hands
  back a `deadpool-postgres` pool bound to it; `Drop` closes the pool and drops
  the database (`DROP DATABASE … WITH (FORCE)` on a dedicated teardown thread,
  since `Drop` is sync and may run inside the tokio runtime). Full isolation —
  including DDL and `information_schema` introspection — so tests run in
  parallel with no shared state. The base connection is read from `DATABASE_URL`
  (the same variable CI sets) with a local default. Three integration tests
  assert a usable database (DDL + CRUD), cross-database isolation, and that the
  database is gone after teardown; all pass against a clean `postgres:16`. Note:
  running locally needs a reachable Postgres with `CREATEDB` rights — set
  `DATABASE_URL` accordingly (a fresh `postgres:16`, e.g. via Docker, avoids the
  glibc collation-version mismatch that a system Postgres upgraded across glibc
  releases will otherwise raise on `CREATE DATABASE`).

- Decided the async runtime and pinned core deps (Phase 0). The workspace runs
  on the **tokio** multi-threaded runtime; every async trait in the design is
  expressed with `async_trait` over it. Chose **tokio-postgres +
  deadpool-postgres** as the Postgres driver rather than sqlx — `sc-query`
  already renders a `Statement` into `(sql, binds)`, so sqlx's compile-time
  query macros add no value, while tokio-postgres gives native `$n` binding and
  row streaming that map directly onto the design's `RowStream`, keeping the
  dependency graph minimal. Added a single `[workspace.dependencies]` block to
  the root `Cargo.toml` pinning `tokio`, `async-trait`, `serde`/`serde_json`,
  `uuid`, `argon2` (stable 0.5; 0.6 is only an RC), `tokio-postgres` (with the
  `uuid`/`chrono`/`serde_json` `ToSql`/`FromSql` features), `deadpool-postgres`,
  and `chrono`/`rust_decimal` (temporal + decimal backing for the `Value` enum).
  Wired tokio into the `saltcorn` binary (`#[tokio::main] async fn main`) so the
  runtime decision is exercised, not just declared. New `core_deps` integration
  test in `sc-cli` asserts each core dep is pinned once in
  `[workspace.dependencies]`, that the driver is tokio-postgres and not sqlx,
  and drives a `#[tokio::test]` end to end.

- Repo hygiene (Phase 0): added `rustfmt.toml` (stable-only options, edition
  pinned to 2024, `max_width = 100`, Unix newlines) so `cargo fmt --check` on a
  stable toolchain matches the workspace. Added a GitHub Actions CI skeleton
  (`.github/workflows/ci.yml`) with three jobs — `fmt` (`cargo fmt --check`),
  `clippy` (`cargo clippy --all-targets -D warnings`), and `test` (`cargo test`
  against a real Postgres 16 service, ready for the integration harness) — with
  build caching and superseded-run cancellation. Extended `.gitignore` to cover
  Node/frontend artifacts (`node_modules/`, `dist/`, `build/`, bundler debug
  logs, `.env*`, `.DS_Store`) for the React apps served by `sc-server`. Added a
  `repo_hygiene` integration test in `sc-cli` that walks up to the workspace
  root and asserts these artifacts exist and declare their required gates
  (`clippy.toml` was already present from the `sc-error` work).
- Implemented `sc-error` (Phase 0, layer 0): a single `Error` enum with coarse,
  location-based variants (`NotFound`, `Invalid`, `Config`, `Database`, `Query`,
  `Auth`, `File`, `Serde`, `Internal`, and a `Context` variant that preserves a
  wrapped source), a `Result<T, E = Error>` alias, and per-variant constructors.
  Added a `Context` extension trait (`.context()` / `.with_context()`) for both
  `Result` and `Option` that keeps the underlying error as a `std::error::Error`
  source chain, plus `bail!` / `ensure!` macros and a `From<std::io::Error>`
  conversion. Enforced principle 5 mechanically: `[workspace.lints.clippy]` denies
  `unwrap_used`/`expect_used`, each member crate opts in via `[lints] workspace =
  true`, and `clippy.toml` exempts test code. Unit + doc tests cover the source
  chain, lazy `with_context`, macros, and `Send + Sync`.
- Created the Cargo workspace with the MVP crate skeletons (Phase 0). Root
  `Cargo.toml` defines shared package metadata (`workspace.package`) and internal
  path dependencies (`workspace.dependencies`) so the strict layering from the
  technical design (§2) is expressed in the dependency graph. Member crates:
  `sc-error`, `sc-query`, `sc-db`, `sc-db-postgres`, `sc-types`, `sc-catalog`,
  `sc-auth`, `sc-files`, `sc-api`, `sc-app`, `sc-server` (libs) and `sc-cli`
  (binary, built as `saltcorn`). Each crate is a compiling stub with a smoke test;
  `cargo build --workspace` and `cargo test --workspace` pass.
